        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>out_peer_prio</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the cooperative chunk budget (us) for <computeroutput>task_idx</computeroutput> in <computeroutput>sched</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns the smallest <computeroutput>sched-&gt;max_wait_ms[prio] * 1000</computeroutput> among all participating peer tasks <computeroutput>j != task_idx</computeroutput> (any non-SUSPENDED peer that is currently alive or executed at least one profiled step in <computeroutput>mgr</computeroutput>). Returns <computeroutput>UINT32_MAX</computeroutput> when uncontended or out of range.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>mgr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional profiler manager (used to include completed peers). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sched</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Scheduler instance. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>task_idx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Task slot index in <computeroutput>sched-&gt;tasks</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>out_peer_prio</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional output receiving the constraining peer priority (0xFF if none). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Allowed cooperative chunk duration in microseconds, or UINT32_MAX if unbounded. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
